  "header": {
    "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: on berlin three pairs of stochastic squads, 7 km apart (beyond any sensor), each a BLUE observer and a RED target standing still in the open: 100 m (eyes only), 2100 m (the observer carries OPTICS) and 2500 m (eyes only). Judge: N-1's curve P(r) = 0.9 * 2^-(r / (R50 * sqrt(men / 9)))^2 per second (R50: eye 400 m, optics 1200 m) accumulates into a level; at level 1 a contact is reported into the observer's own contact pool. The 100 m and 2100 m contacts appear inside the window the curve predicts (the step counts are in the row names); the 2500 m target, beyond the naked eye's reach (the soldiers' own vision range), is never contacted. Fail: a contact far out of the window, or beyond the eye's reach. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh agg-detect-by-range"
  },
